# The image's own default for the schema GTK actually reads.
#
# Measured on 8 September: GTK3 takes its widget theme from
# `org.gnome.desktop.interface` whenever these schemas are installed - they are,
# 37 of them - and falls back to the SCHEMA'S DEFAULT rather than to the
# `gtk-3.0/settings.ini` we write. With no value set that default is 'Adwaita',
# so a GTK3 app on a fresh image was in stock Adwaita even though the Arlen theme
# was built, installed and named in the settings file.
#
# The shell writes this key on every theme apply, which covers a running desktop.
# This covers what happens before that and if it ever fails: the first GTK3 window
# of a session, a session where the shell did not start, an app launched from a
# tty. An override changes the DEFAULT only, so a value the person sets themselves
# still wins - which is the layering we want rather than a value we force.
#
# Sorted last on purpose: Debian ships 10_gsettings-desktop-schemas.gschema.override
# and the highest-numbered file wins.
#
# Font deliberately absent. Ours resolves to Inter, which is not on this image,
# and naming a font the machine does not have is the same untruth as naming an
# icon theme it does not have - `generate_gtk_settings_ini` omits that key for
# exactly this reason.
[org.gnome.desktop.interface]
gtk-theme='Arlen'
color-scheme='prefer-dark'
